{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Peter Visits Vanessa in San Francisco", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "You're Leaving Tomorrow!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 4, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Present vs. Present Continuous Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Present tense to talk about: <br><ul><li>a routine action or specific action that happens regularly </li><li>a general truth</li><li>to give personal information </li> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": " You can use expressions of frequency like <span class=\"italic\">every day</span> or <span class=\"italic\">always</span> with the Simple Present. <br><br> You form the Present Continuous with the verb <span class=\"strong\">to be + verb-ing</span>. <br><br> You use the Present Continuous tense to talk about:  <ul><li>a current event or action happening around now  </li><li>events that <span class=\"strong\">are going to happen</span> soon (future plans)  </li>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">right now </span> or<span class=\"italic\"> later </span> with the Present Continuous. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I understand what you mean.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You're leaving tomorrow!</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">What do you mean by that?</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I am looking forward to coming back next year.</span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "&nbsp;", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Review of Modals", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You often use a modal like <span class=\"italic\">can, may, could</span> or <span class=\"italic\">would</span> to ask for permission.  <br><br>  You also use the modals <span class=\"italic\">may, might</span> or <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to show possibility. <br> <br>The modal <span class=\"italic\">could</span> is used to ask for clarification.<br><br>Modals are placed before a verb in the base form. The verb does not change.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Can I come back next year?  (permission)</span> ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You could come back this summer.  (possibility)</span> ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Could you explain what you mean (by that)?  (clarification) </span> ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "police station", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the place where police officers work ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm in a police station. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words to review.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "decorated", "type": "name"}, {"content": "made to look better by adding things", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: City Hall is decorated with flashing lights. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cable car", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a type of vehicle used in San Francisco that is pulled up hill by cable", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We got into an accident with a couple of cable cars", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ride", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a trip to a place in a car or another vehicle", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A kind taxi driver offered me a ride.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "took ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the verb <span class=\"italic\">to take</span> in the Simple Past tense", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I took a bus from the airport.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think of a destination. It can be a place you went to or a place you want to go to.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a dialogue. Talk about what you did on the trip.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Explain what you liked best.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about other things you enjoyed.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Say what you didn't like.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your dialogue to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Change roles.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a dialogue of 8-10 lines about an experience on a trip.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I say what I liked the most.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I say what I enjoyed.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I say what I didn't like.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I practice the dialogue with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override"